Regression: when the uplink is down at start time (no default route in
ubus status), pbr.start_service emits warningUplinkDown and returns a
PARTIAL result with { deferredToBoot: true, ifacesTriggers: ... } on
purpose — the wrapper still emits _pbr_ifaces_triggers so the per-iface
procd triggers are registered, and procd's boot retry kicks in on the
next interface.*.up event (see issue #113). service_started must NOT
emit "FAILED TO START" or "Check the output of nft -c -f" in that
path, because nothing actually failed; we're deferring to boot mode.

